            "value": [
              {
                "dsDescriptionValue": {
                  "typeName": "dsDescriptionValue",
                  "multiple": false,
                  "typeClass": "primitive",
                  "value": "Data for Figure 5 of \"Quantification of deep medullary veins at 7 T brain MRI\", DOI: <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00330-016-4220-y\">10.1007/s00330-016-4220-y</a>. \n\nCaption: Venous density map of 30 aged individuals (17 male; 70 ± 3.8 years), where all reconstructed deep medullary veins are transformed to the MNI152 template. Each reconstructed vein consists of many individual points (originating from the vessel tracking algorithm), approximately one point per venous voxel. The given density denotes the number of vein points within a 15 mm radius of each MNI152 template voxel."
                }
              }
